# Daily PROD backup for the `backup` service (busybox crond, UTC). Edit the schedule here; Dokploy redeploys on push.
# The file is copied into the image at build time (deploy/compose.yaml), so crond reads a root-owned crontab.
# minute hour day month weekday  command
# 08:30 UTC = 03:30 Bogotá. The job logs to the container's stdout (PID 1) so it shows in the Dokploy logs.
# backup-prod.sh takes the lock shared with `migrate` itself (BACKUP_LOCK_FILE, waits BACKUP_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS) and
# gives up with an error if it cannot get it; the next try is tomorrow. Do not add a lock here: it would deadlock.
30 8 * * * exec >/proc/1/fd/1 2>&1; BACKUP_REASON=daily exec sh /scripts/backup-prod.sh
